   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Making and answering suggestions",
     "texto": [
      "To suggest a plan together:\n\n- **¿Y si** vamos al cine?\n- **¿Qué te parece si** cenamos fuera?\n- **¿Te apetece** dar un paseo? / **¿Te apetece que** demos un paseo?\n- **Podríamos** ir a la playa.\n\nTo accept: **Vale.** **Estupendo.** **Buena idea.** **Me apunto.** With **Bueno, si insistes…** you accept reluctantly.\n\nTo decline politely, say thank you, give an excuse or suggest something else:\n\n- **No, gracias, es que** estoy cansado.\n- **Prefiero** quedarme en casa.\n- **Mejor otro día**, ¿vale?"
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Indicative, conditional and subjunctive",
     "texto": [
      "Each formula takes a different tense:\n\n- **¿Y si** / **¿Qué te parece si** + present **indicative**: *¿Y si pedimos una pizza?*\n- **Podríamos** + infinitive: a soft suggestion, with the **conditional**.\n- **¿Te apetece** + infinitive, when you talk about the other person: *¿Te apetece ir al cine?*\n- **¿Te apetece que** + **subjunctive**, when you include others: *¿Te apetece que vayamos al cine?*\n- **Prefiero** + infinitive, with the same subject. **Prefiero que** + subjunctive, with another subject: *Prefiero que vayamos solos.*\n\nTo accept or decline, a short phrase is enough: **me apunto**, **mejor otro día**."
     ],
